---
/** The app's own marks (ProvenanceMark.kt): solid = said, hollow = inferred. The copy is the app's: "From the
 *  transcript" / "Generated from your memory". */
---
<ul class="prov" aria-label="Two example memory items">
  <li class="card">
    <span class="mark solid" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div>
      <strong>Priya will send the revised budget by Friday.</strong>
      <small><b>Said</b> · from the transcript · 14:32</small>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li class="card">
    <span class="mark hollow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div>
      <strong>The budget is probably tied to the Q4 headcount decision.</strong>
      <small><b>Inferred</b> · generated from your memory</small>
    </div>
  </li>
</ul>
<p class="legend">A solid mark means someone said it, and the item links to the moment. A hollow mark means Remana inferred it, and says so.</p>
<style>
  .prov { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--space-md); max-width: 44rem; }
  .prov li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 20px 1fr; gap: var(--space-lg); align-items: start; padding: var(--space-lg) var(--space-xl); }
  .mark { width: 20px; height: 20px; border-radius: 50%; margin-top: 2px; }
  .solid { background: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--accent-soft); }
  .hollow { border: 3px solid var(--mark-hollow); }
  .prov li div { display: grid; gap: var(--space-xs); }
  .prov strong { font-size: var(--text-lg); line-height: 1.35; }
  .prov small { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: var(--text-sm); } .prov b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .legend { margin-top: var(--space-lg); max-width: 44rem; }
</style>
